{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791806159,"nonce":"AExs3A7oRx/6epew4jEWKBfm6CY=","title":"Associated sizing issue: e8a1b50; API milestone f564eea.","message":"Populated InputOtp slots using the default macOS --font-mono stack resolve SF Mono. Swash rasterizes this font's unhinted CFF outlines in font units instead of pixels: digit 3 at 32 px produces 1020 x 1503 pixels (19 x 25 when hinting is enabled). The font's units-per-em is 2048 in both ttf-parser and Swash, so this is not integer rounding or a UI layout error.\n\nOnce enough of these glyphs are prepared, the coverage atlas reaches 4096 x 4096. blinc_abi's display-list retry clears the atlas after its second failed attempt, while retaining previously emitted glyph records. Its atlas export then reports the valid dimensions/revision but returns only zero coverage. All text disappears from the frame, including unrelated headings and editable fields.\n\nReproduced in Ash interpreter and hybrid, and in a standalone Rust Swash probe without Ash. Swash 0.1.15, 0.1.17, 0.1.18 and 0.1.19 all reproduce the unhinted CFF scaling error; hint(true) produces correctly scaled glyphs. The active production dependency remains 0.1.19; no dependency downgrade was retained.\n\nEvidence: .ashui/snapshots/size-native-debug-diag.log, component-size-pixels-baseline.log, cff-probe.log, cff-probe-15.log and cff-probe-17.log. Temporary diagnostic bridges and extracted font bytes are under /private/tmp and are not shipped.\n\nFollow-up: fix CFF scaling in the native text engine and ensure a failed atlas retry cannot clear glyphs still referenced by returned records. Use a supported TrueType monospace font for the component size gallery until this native issue is fixed; component CSS continues to use the theme's font token.","files":null}]}